<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1944</h1><p class="ref-lede">1944 in world history: 69 events, 17 births, 28 deaths, 6 states founded and 11 that came to an end. 725 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a><a href="/years/1941">1941</a><a href="/years/1942">1942</a><a href="/years/1943">1943</a><a href="/years/1944" aria-current="page">1944</a><a href="/years/1945">1945</a><a href="/years/1946">1946</a><a href="/years/1947">1947</a><a href="/years/1948">1948</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-22">22 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Allied troops land at Anzio</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Shingle, Allied forces landed behind German lines south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, hoping to outflank the Gustav Line. Quickly contained, they endured four months of hard fighting before breaking out.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-27">27 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Siege of Leningrad is lifted after 872 days</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet offensives drove German forces back from Leningrad, ending a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> that began in September 1941. Some 800,000 or more civilians died, most from starvation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-24">24 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Allied prisoners break out in the 'Great Escape'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">That night 76 airmen crawled through a tunnel out of Stalag Luft III in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagan">Sagan</a>. Only three reached safety; on Hitler's orders, 50 of those recaptured were shot.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-6">6 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Allied armies land in Normandy on D-Day</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">About 156,000 Allied troops landed by sea and air on the Normandy coast. The invasion opened the long-awaited second front against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-10">10 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">SS troops massacre the village of Oradour-sur-Glane</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waffen-ss">Waffen-SS</a> unit killed 643 people in the French village, shooting the men and burning women and children in the church. The ruins are preserved as a memorial.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-17">17 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Iceland becomes a republic</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thingvellir">Þingvellir</a>, the site of its ancient assembly, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iceland">Iceland</a> ended its union with the Danish crown and proclaimed a republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> was then under German occupation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-22">22 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt signs the G.I. Bill</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Servicemen's Readjustment Act gave veterans college tuition, low-cost home loans and unemployment pay. Millions took up its benefits, expanding higher education and home ownership.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-6">6 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fire sweeps a circus big top in Hartford, killing 167</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Ringling Bros. tent, waterproofed with paraffin and petrol, caught fire during a matinee in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hartford-connecticut">Hartford, Connecticut</a>. At least 167 people died, many of them children, prompting tighter fire-safety rules.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-20">20 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Stauffenberg's bomb fails to kill Hitler</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claus-von-stauffenberg">Claus von Stauffenberg</a> left a briefcase bomb at Hitler's Wolf's Lair headquarters, but Hitler survived. The plotters were executed and thousands more were arrested in the reprisals that followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warsaw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-1">1 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Warsaw Uprising begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Polish Home Army rose against the German occupiers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>. After 63 days, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> halted across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>, the uprising was crushed and the city systematically destroyed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-4">4 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Anne Frank and her family are arrested in Amsterdam</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German police raided the secret annexe at Prinsengracht 263, arresting the Frank family and four others. Anne died in Bergen-Belsen in early 1945; her diary became a classic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a> testimony.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-12">12 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">SS troops massacre villagers at Sant'Anna di Stazzema</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waffen-ss">Waffen-SS</a> soldiers killed some 560 civilians, many of them women and children, in the Tuscan village of Sant'Anna di Stazzema. It was one of the worst atrocities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy">German occupation of Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy">German occupation of Italy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-25">25 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Paris is liberated from German occupation</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">French and American troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and the German commander, General von Choltitz, surrendered, having ignored Hitler's order to destroy the city. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">De Gaulle</a> led a victory march the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rhine" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-17">17 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Operation Market Garden begins in the Netherlands</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 35,000 Allied airborne troops landed to seize bridges leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. The operation failed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnhem">Arnhem</a>, ending hopes of finishing the war by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas">Christmas</a> 1944.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-20">20 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US forces land on Leyte as MacArthur returns</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops landed on Leyte, and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douglas-macarthur">Douglas MacArthur</a> waded ashore to fulfil his 1942 promise to return to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. Days later, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leyte">Battle of Leyte</a> Gulf crippled the Japanese navy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-25">25 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan launches its first organised kamikaze attacks</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leyte">Battle of Leyte</a> Gulf, Japanese pilots deliberately crashed their aircraft into American ships, sinking the escort carrier St. Lo. Suicide attacks became a central Japanese tactic for the rest of the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-16">16 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany launches the Battle of the Bulge</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces attacked through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a>, catching the Americans by surprise. The offensive was contained within weeks and used up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s last reserves in the west.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/operation-bagration" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-bagration.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/operation-bagration">Operation Bagration</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Bagration was the Soviet summer offensive of 1944 in Belarus, launched on 22–23 June.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/brazzaville-conference" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brazzaville-conference.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/brazzaville-conference">Brazzaville Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Brazzaville Conference was a meeting of Free French colonial officials opened by Charles de Gaulle at Brazzaville in January 1944.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-imphal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-imphal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-imphal">Battle of Imphal</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Imphal was fought from March to July 1944 around the town of Imphal in north-eastern India, when the Japanese Fifteenth Army attempted to invade India from Burma.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kohima" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kohima.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kohima">Battle of Kohima</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Kohima was fought from April to June 1944 at Kohima in the Naga Hills of north-eastern India, as part of the Japanese offensive against India.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tali-ihantala" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tali-ihantala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tali-ihantala">Battle of Tali-Ihantala</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tali-Ihantala, fought from 25 June to 9 July 1944 north-east of Viipuri, was the largest battle ever fought in the Nordic countries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tannenberg-line" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tannenberg-line.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tannenberg-line">Battle of Tannenberg Line</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tannenberg Line was fought in July and August 1944 at the Sinimäed hills near Narva in north-eastern Estonia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thiaroye-massacre" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thiaroye-massacre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/thiaroye-massacre">Thiaroye massacre</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Thiaroye massacre took place on 1 December 1944 at the Thiaroye military camp near Dakar, when French troops fired on West African tirailleurs, recently released prisoners of war returned from France, who were protesting over unpaid wages and allowances.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/liberation-of-paris">Liberation of Paris</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Liberation of Paris was the freeing of the French capital from German occupation in August 1944.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/20-july-plot" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/20-july-plot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/20-july-plot">20 July plot</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 20 July plot was a failed attempt on 20 July 1944 to assassinate Adolf Hitler and overthrow the Nazi government, made by members of the German resistance, mainly Wehrmacht officers.</p></div></li></ol></section>
