<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Guatemala.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Guatemala</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The October Revolution opens a decade of democratic reform</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-finland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Finland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Finland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Continuation War ends with an armistice and the loss of Karelia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Ankole.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Ankole</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Charles Gasyonga II succeeds Kahaya II</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/liberia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Liberia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liberia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">William Tubman begins a presidency lasting until 1971</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-west-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20West%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French West Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">French troops fire on tirailleurs at the Thiaroye camp near Dakar</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/capitalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Capitalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Capitalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Friedrich Hayek argues in The Road to Serfdom that economic freedom is a requisite of political freedom</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/nelson-mandela"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nelson%20Mandela.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nelson Mandela</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mandela helps to found the African National Congress Youth League and sits on its executive committee</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/independent-state-of-croatia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Independent%20State%20of%20Croatia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Independent State of Croatia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Lorković-Vokić coup against Pavelić fails and its conspirators are executed</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/vichy-france"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vichy%20France.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vichy France</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the liberation of Paris, Pétain and his ministers are taken to Sigmaringen by German forces</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/bayeux-tapestry"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Bayeux%20Tapestry.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Bayeux Tapestry</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Gestapo took it to the Louvre, and Himmler's order to remove it to safety came too late</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/chamorro-people"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Chamorro%20people.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Chamorro people</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">American forces recaptured Guam, a victory marked by Liberation Day</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Hungary%20(1920-1946).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Germany occupies Hungary in March, and in October overthrows Horthy and installs Ferenc Szálasi of the Arrow Cross Party</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/korea-under-japanese-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Korea%20under%20Japanese%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Korea under Japanese rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan begins conscripting Korean men into the Imperial Japanese Army and the military industrial sector</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/paris"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Paris.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Paris</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The city is liberated on 25 August after four years of German occupation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-iwo-jima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Iwo%20Jima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Iwo Jima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lieutenant General Tadamichi Kuribayashi is assigned to command the defence of Iwo Jima, and the American air raids and shore bombardment begin on 15 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-kohima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Kohima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Kohima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Imperial General Headquarters approves the U-Go offensive into India</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-kohima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Kohima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Kohima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Japanese 31st Division crosses the Chindwin and spends six days fighting at Sangshak, which delays it by a week</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-kohima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Kohima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Kohima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The siege of Kohima begins and the garrison is driven into a small perimeter on Garrison Hill</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-kohima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Kohima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Kohima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A tank dragged to the summit destroys the Japanese bunkers at the tennis court, clearing Kohima Ridge</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-kohima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Kohima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Kohima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Troops from Kohima and Imphal meet at Milestone 109, ending the Siege of Imphal</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-kohima"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Kohima.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Kohima</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Satō is removed from command and the Japanese offensive is broken off</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hitler first outlines a counter-offensive to his generals on 16 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 16 December the Germans open the offensive with a 90-minute barrage and achieve total surprise</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 17 December prisoners are shot near Baugnez in the Malmedy massacre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 19 December the 101st Airborne Division reaches Bastogne by truck, and the town is cut off on 20 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 24 December the furthest German advance is stopped at Foy-Notre-Dame by the U.S. 2nd Armored Division</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-bulge"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Bulge.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Bulge</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 26 December the lead element of Patton's Third Army reaches Bastogne from the south and ends the siege</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/normandy-landings"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Normandy%20landings.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Normandy landings</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 4 June Eisenhower meets Group Captain James Stagg, whose forecast of improving weather leads him to go ahead on 6 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/normandy-landings"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Normandy%20landings.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Normandy landings</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 6 June airborne troops land after midnight and the amphibious landings on the five beaches begin about 06:30</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/normandy-landings"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Normandy%20landings.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Normandy landings</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 12 June the five beachheads are connected</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/normandy-landings"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Normandy%20landings.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Normandy landings</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Caen is completely captured</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/normandy-landings"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Normandy%20landings.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Normandy landings</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">German forces retreat east across the Seine, closing Operation Overlord</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/warsaw"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Warsaw.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Warsaw</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Warsaw Uprising is crushed and the Germans raze the city</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/mogao-caves"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mogao%20Caves.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mogao Caves</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Research Institute of Dunhuang Art, later the Dunhuang Academy, was set up at the site</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/quit-india-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Quit%20India%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Quit India movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Gandhi is released on account of his health and demands the release of the Congress leadership</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/social-darwinism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Social%20Darwinism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Social Darwinism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Richard Hofstadter publishes Social Darwinism in American Thought, which popularises the term in the United States</span></li></ul></section>
